-- title:
--   Vanishing on the zero component forces Gauss nonunit
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero level $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$; assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\mathfrak{P}$ be a model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` (the project's structure packaging a proper, flat, normal integral model of $X_H(M)$ over $R p$ together with its geometric companion models and chart pinnings). Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $(p : \overline{\mathbb{Q}}) \in A.\mathrm{nonunits}$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho : R p \to A$ satisfy $A.\mathrm{subtype} \circ \rho = \mathrm{algebraMap}$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` characterised by: $f \in W_0$ iff $f \cdot a' = a$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \mathbb{Q}$ for some power series $a, a'$ with coefficients in the subring of rationals with denominators coprime to $p$, the coefficientwise reduction of $a'$ modulo $p$ being nonzero — i.e. $W_0$ is the Gauss valuation ring. Assume the preimage of the $\infty$-chart open $(\iota_{\mathrm{Inf}})_*\top$ under the composite $\mathfrak{P}.\mathrm{efib} \circ \mathfrak{P}.\mathrm{comp}\ 0 \circ \mathrm{pullback.fst}$ into the fibre over $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the residue map $\mathrm{residue} \circ \rho$ is nonempty. Then for every $b$ in `chartAlgInf p (ΓM M H) hj`, the $R p$-subalgebra of the function field generated by $j^{-1}$: if the section determined by $b$ on that open, pulled back along this composite and transported to the function field of the curve model $\mathfrak{P}.\mathrm{Mfib}$ by the inverse of its `ffEquiv`, is zero, then the image of $b$ in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` lies in $W_0.\mathrm{nonunits}$, the maximal ideal of the Gauss valuation ring.
--
--   This is the geometric half of the computation that reads off the $q$-expansion of a pole-chart function of the integral model along the $\infty$-branch in characteristic $p$: vanishing on the distinguished component of the fibre is converted into positive Gauss valuation, hence into vanishing of the reduced $q$-expansion. It feeds the statement identifying the transported germ with the coefficientwise reduction of the $q$-expansion in the case $p \,\|\, M$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_mem_nonunits_gauss_of_ffEquiv_symm_germToFunctionField_app_comp_zero_eq_zero.lean

